Cell[TextData[{
 "DON\[CloseCurlyQuote]T DO THIS: You CAN assign values to things that look \
like naked extended formals, but it is highly discouraged. They\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]re not extended. They appear in the ",
 StyleBox["User", "Input"],
 " classification. The only real extended formals are constructed ones \
(examples below). ",
 StyleBox["There is no such thing as a naked, literal extended formal",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ". The constructor will protect constructed extended formals, as we see \
below, so you can\[CloseCurlyQuote]t assign values to them after-the-fact. "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.979920151491296*^9, 3.979920224886882*^9}, {
